{"name":"Buckingham Gardens","hex":"#89a068","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gardens","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of garden"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of garden"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gardens"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buckingham","blocks":[{"text":"Buckingham is a market town in north Buckinghamshire, England, close to the borders with Northamptonshire and Oxfordshire. The civil parish of Buckingham had a population of 14,294 at the 2021 census. The town lies approximately 12 miles (19 km) west of Milton Keynes, 19 miles (31 km) south-east of Banbury and 24 miles (39 km) north-east of Oxford."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Buckingham_Town_Hall_%28geograph_1486407%29.jpg/330px-Buckingham_Town_Hall_%28geograph_1486407%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckingham"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Buckingham_OldCountyGaol02.JPG/500px-Buckingham_OldCountyGaol02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Buckingham_OldCountyGaol02.JPG/1280px-Buckingham_OldCountyGaol02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u